  "title": "Chapter 14 – Nutrition & Dietetics",
  "order": 14,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "g7hydbk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Nutrients are categorized into macronutrients (carbohydrates, proteins, fats) and micronutrients (vitamins, minerals).",
        "A balanced diet provides essential energy, amino acids, essential fatty acids, vitamins, and minerals in adequate proportions.",
        "Vitamins are classified into fat-soluble (A, D, E, K) and water-soluble (B-complex and C) groups.",
        "Malnutrition covers both undernutrition (e.g., Kwashiorkor and Marasmus) and overnutrition/obesity.",
        "Therapeutic diets are modified normal diets tailored to meet specific clinical and medical requirements of patients."
      ],
      "id": "vihfolx"
    },
